# Authentication

## Credentials and endpoint

Use a Control user personal access token (PAT) or service-account bearer token.
An Ingress integration token and a dataset-scoped publisher token cannot
substitute for Control credentials.

```shell
export ONPAGER_ENDPOINT="https://onpager.example.test/control"
export ONPAGER_TOKEN="<Control bearer token>"
```

```terraform
provider "onpager" {}
```

`endpoint` is an HTTP(S) base URL with an optional reverse-proxy path prefix. It
must not contain embedded credentials, query parameters or a fragment. Resource
requests append `/v1`. HTTPS verifies server certificates.

Provider `endpoint` and `token` arguments take precedence over their respective
environment variables. Omitted or `null` arguments use the environment fallback;
explicit empty strings are errors. Values must be known when Terraform configures
the provider. An unknown expression produces a diagnostic instead of falling
back to environment credentials.

For explicit arguments:

```terraform
provider "onpager" {
  endpoint = var.onpager_endpoint
  token    = var.onpager_token
}
```

Declare the token input variable with `sensitive = true`. Configure credentials
through the environment or an existing secret-management integration.

